---
/**
 * The reference layer, and the surface AI search actually quotes.
 *
 * Objections that BLOCK the form are handled inline beside the form; this is
 * where the rest lives. Answers are written to be self-contained and quotable,
 * because a paragraph that only makes sense in context is useless to both a
 * skim-reader and a citation.
 *
 * The `name="faq"` attribute is deliberately absent: an exclusive accordion
 * closes the answer someone is comparing against, which on a trust page is
 * exactly the wrong behaviour.
 */
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { MONEY, PLACE } from '../lib/claims';

export const QA: [string, string][] = [
  [
    'What does "verified halal" mean here, exactly?',
    "A person on our team read the restaurant's halal certificate and recorded the result of seven separate checks — the issuer, the legal name, the address, the certificate number, the dates, what it covers, and whether it has been used elsewhere. We record who checked it and when. The badge on a listing is that record, and you can open the certificate behind it. We don't certify food ourselves and we don't make religious rulings.",
  ],
  [
    'Is the whole restaurant certified, or just the meat?',
    "We check what the certificate actually covers, and the scope has to cover the whole establishment or the kitchen. A certificate that covers only a meat supplier fails that check and the restaurant is not listed. This is the single most common mix-up in the industry — a real supplier certificate, shown at the counter, taken to mean the kitchen is certified.",
  ],
  [
    'Whose standard do you use — is it zabiha?',
    "Ours isn't a standard, it's a check. We verify the certificate is real, currently in force, and issued by a body on our accepted registry — then we print which body issued it. Issuers differ, and Muslims differ on them. That judgement is yours, which is why the issuer's name is on the listing instead of being hidden behind a label of our own. We don't rank or score certifying bodies.",
  ],
  [
    'Do you certify food yourselves?',
    'No. Never. We read certificates issued by others and record what they say. Halal Goes does not itself certify food.',
  ],
  [
    'What happens if a certificate expires?',
    "The restaurant comes off the app until it's renewed — there's no grace period. We don't show a warning badge on food, because an expired certificate means our information has lapsed, not that anything is wrong with what the kitchen is cooking. When a new certificate is approved the restaurant goes back up automatically; the lapse isn't a punishment.",
  ],
  [
    'Who actually checks it — a person, or software?',
    "A person reads the document and signs off, and we record their name against the date. Two of the seven checks are computed by the server instead — whether the dates are valid, and whether that certificate number is already in use by a different restaurant — and no admin can override either of those. Nothing is ever auto-approved on a timer.",
  ],
  [
    'What will it cost to order?',
    `The menu price plus a delivery fee, and the amount you're shown before you pay is the amount that gets charged — no fee appears afterwards. ${MONEY.tipToRider} of any tip goes to your rider, and so does ${MONEY.deliveryFeeToRider} of the delivery fee. Tipping is optional and starts at zero; there's no pre-selected amount.`,
  ],
  [
    'Where and when do you launch?',
    `${PLACE.province} first. We're pre-launch — this page is a waitlist, not a download, and there's nothing to install yet. Leave your email and we'll write once, the day we open in your area.`,
  ],
  [
    'What will you do with my email address?',
    "Write to you when we open in your area, and after that only when there are newly verified kitchens near you. We don't sell it and we don't pass it to restaurants. Every email has one-click unsubscribe.",
  ],
];
---
<section class="section faq">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="mkt-h2 faq-h" data-reveal>Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" data-reveal-group>
      {QA.map(([q, a], i) => (
        <details open={i === 0} data-reveal>
          <summary>
            <span>{q}</span>
            <Icon name="chevron-down" size="md" color="var(--text-tertiary)" class="chev" />
          </summary>
          <p>{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq { background: var(--surface-base); }
  .faq-h { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .faq-list { max-width: 720px; }

  details { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-decorative); }
  details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-decorative); }
  summary {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px 0; cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
    font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary > span:first-child { flex: 1; }
  .chev { flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 2px; transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-standard); }
  details[open] .chev { transform: rotate(180deg); }
  details p {
    margin: 0; padding: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 62ch;
  }
</style>
